"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Wall of Wood","oracle_id":"aa5e6894-8c97-46f8-a0fd-07c6db51e9a7","oracle_text":"Defender (This creature can't attack.)","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-07-13","toughness":"3","type_line":"Creature — Wall"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Overprotect, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"129476ae-9dab-4e04-8e8e-f249afd56ff9","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Maha’s last ability overwrites all previous effects that set those creatures’ base toughness to specific values. Any toughness-setting effects that start to apply afterward will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"129476ae-9dab-4e04-8e8e-f249afd56ff9","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage remains marked on creatures until the turn ends. If Fecund Greenshell’s second ability stops applying (because Fecund Greenshell leaves the battlefield or loses its abilities or because you no longer control ten or more lands), then any creatures that needed the toughness bonus to stay alive will die.","oracle_id":"a090be5a-b0f2-4c17-8f7d-e742f9de8f6b","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Fecund Greenshell’s last ability checks the power and toughness of a creature only at the moment it enters. If it enters with counters, those counters are included. Static abilities that modify the power and toughness of creatures you control (such as Fecund Greenshell’s own second ability) are also included. If that creature’s toughness is greater than its power when it enters, the ability will still trigger and resolve normally regardless of what happens to that creature after that.","oracle_id":"a090be5a-b0f2-4c17-8f7d-e742f9de8f6b","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the top card of your library is a land card, you may choose to put it into your hand rather than onto the battlefield tapped.","oracle_id":"a090be5a-b0f2-4c17-8f7d-e742f9de8f6b","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
